<spell-notebook "code theming">
	<header level="1">
		Code
		<header>Code shows a block of source code coloured by its language, from the element's own text or a file on
              this site.</>
	</>
	<code-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-code-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every block of
			code), or on the box through `::part(box)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias. Never set the `--_ui-code-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.

			The colours are one token per highlight group -- `keyword`, `string`, `number`, `comment`, `title`, `type`, `attr`,
			`meta`, `addition`, `deletion` -- each with a light and a dark value, so code follows the colour scheme. Style the
			pieces with `::part()`: `box`, `pre`, `code` and `copy`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every block of code on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-code-radius: 0;
			  --ui-code-keyword: var(--ui-purple);
			}
			/* one kind, bigger */
			ui-code.listing {
			  --ui-code-font-size: 1em;
			}
			ui-code::part(copy) {
			  font-weight: bold;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-code" playground>
				<ui-code language="typescript">
					<script type="text/plain">
						const greeting = "hello"
						// one line each
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Code is ours, not Fomantic's:  the theme menu in the header changes the page around it.  Its colours
			follow the light or dark scheme.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
